set and builds its tools, and the guards run a call the model makes](diagrams/general-packs-diagrams-2.svg)\nsrc/docs/GOAL.md:26: | 4 | **Tool design** | About 140 described tools in fifteen packs (counted 2026-11-13), their result and error texts as \u0060ToolMessage\u0060 templates (CL3), agent-built tools with approval, guarded results; toolset profiles: a session loads only the toolsets it needs, with only their guides (F5); tools per role (F22): \u0060GetToday\u0060 in every session, documents (PdfPig, OpenXml, ExcelDataReader), blame and history search with arguments as a list, tables, currency at the display rates; web search and page rendering as seams with interchangeable providers, chosen by enums (F32, ADR 0024); a shop\u0027s catalogue read in code (\u0060FindProducts\u0060, F33), a role declaring its own toolsets, and optional toolsets loaded only where an instance has them; deal searches split by kind (\u0060SearchSpecials\u0060, \u0060SearchPromotions\u0060) and a tool argument cut to what may go on (\u0060area\u0060: the town only, F34); tool names unique and MCP-safe through one catalogue, and every pack kept convertible to MCP (CL15, \u0060PackConvertibilityTests\u0060); a tool where it does a prompt\u0027s job better: sums in a calculator pack, not in the model\u0027s head (F35.5, [ADR 0080](adr/0080-a-tool-when-it-improves-the-prompt.md)); tools the page hears: the guide takes a visitor to a section and draws cards and a form in the chat, and plays a recorded demo a turn at a time by showing its turns\u0027 addresses (F117, F127.4, F160, [ADR 0105](adr/0105-the-guide-acts-on-the-page-through-a-tool-the-widget-hears.md)); a lead as a tool, sent once on the visitor\u0027s yes ([ADR 0101](adr/0101-a-lead-is-a-tool-sent-once-on-the-visitors-yes.md)) | Results as tool calls between agents (F39, Phase 6, taking in F8-S4); a tool list frozen per conversation (FX4, Phase 7); each tool\u0027s declared effect (\u0060ToolEffect\u0060) and errors that list every problem at once with the valid options (F41, Phase 7); annotations and output schemas on our MCP server\u0027s tools (F36, Phase 8) | Tool search / on-demand tool loading for large toolsets (F38, when a measured need comes); adding a tool mid-conversation without breaking thinking or the cache (Anthropic\u0027s inline tool blocks, after FX4) |\nsrc/docs/GOAL.md:29: | 7 | **Context engineering** | Oversized results summarised, cut-off tool calls never run (\u0060ToolCallGuards\u0060, CL2); each product carries only its own routing (CL9: the coding agent\u0027s fixed prefix 801 tokens smaller); a shop\u0027s prices read from its catalogue as a short table instead of a model reading its pages (F33); a page\u0027s own data read in code before its text (F35, [ADR 0067](adr/0067-a-pages-own-data-before-its-text.md)); skills read on demand instead of carried in every prompt (F129); a message may carry the page the visitor is reading, one block sent once per page (F115, [ADR 0104](adr/0104-a-message-may-carry-the-page.md)) | Each model\u0027s window and price step as the limits (F15, Phase 9); long chats: clear stale results, summarise, then open a new window, and the context-building step per turn (retrieve, rank, budget) (F9, *Later*, taking in F16\u0027s summariser) | \u2014 |"